      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "The Muslim Community Center Chicago demonstrates consistent operational sustainability backed by robust financial management. In FY2024, the charity brought in <cite id=\"1\">$10,751,849 in total revenue</cite> while maintaining <cite id=\"1\">a 92.7% program expense ratio</cite>, comfortably beating the industry benchmark of 75% [1]. Independent evaluation supports this performance, highlighted by an <cite id=\"2\">overall score of 95.0/100 from Charity Navigator</cite> [2]. Beyond its daily religious and educational programming through the MCC Academy, the organization disbursed <cite id=\"1\">$551,623 in grants in 2023</cite> to support broader relief and partner initiatives [1]."
      ],
      "summary": "Founded in 1969, the Muslim Community Center Chicago operates as a central institutional hub for education, worship, and social services [1, 3]. In FY2024, the organization managed <cite id=\"1\">$10,751,849 in total revenue</cite> to support core operations, including its masjids, the MCC Academy full-time school, and community counseling services [1, 3]. Financial efficiency remains high, with <cite id=\"1\">a program expense ratio of 92.7%</cite>, ensuring that the vast majority of resources directly fund programs [1]. The charity maintains an <cite id=\"2\">overall score of 95.0/100 from Charity Navigator</cite>, backed by high accountability standards [2]. Donors can contribute through <cite id=\"7\">verified zakat-eligible funds</cite> that directly aid community members in need [7]. However, the organization retains substantial cash reserves and currently lacks a documented theory of change [1].",
